# Normalize to LF in the repository, and check out LF everywhere.
#
# This project is developed on Windows but runs on Databricks and is tested under
# WSL, so a CRLF checkout is actively harmful: make reads the Makefile through a
# Linux shell, and a CRLF recipe line fails there. Pinning eol=lf keeps one
# representation everywhere rather than one per contributor's autocrlf setting.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary: never touch these.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.whl binary
*.sas7bdat binary
